  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}.$",
  "worked_solution": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{4{u}_{1}(t)} & =\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{4{u}_{1}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ 4{u}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}} & =4{u}_{1}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
